        <p>These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of <strong>India</strong>, without regard to its conflict of law provisions.</p>
        <p>Any disputes arising out of or in connection with these Terms shall first be attempted to be resolved through good-faith negotiation. If unresolved within 30 days, disputes shall be submitted to binding arbitration in accordance with the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, with the seat of arbitration in <strong>Bengaluru, Karnataka</strong>.</p>
        <p>Notwithstanding the above, either party may seek injunctive or other equitable relief from courts of competent jurisdiction in Bengaluru, Karnataka to prevent any actual or threatened infringement, misappropriation, or violation of intellectual property rights.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Contact Card -->
      <div class="legal-contact-card">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-envelope-open-text fa-2x mb-3" style="opacity: 0.8;"></i>
        <h3>Questions about these Terms?</h3>
        <p>Our legal team is happy to help clarify any section of these Terms of Service.</p>
        <a href="mailto:legal@staynest.in"><i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane me-2"></i>Contact Legal Team</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
